  "mechanism_and_attribution": {
    "CDC20": "Hub gene from human datasets; Cdc20 mRNA increased in CCl4 versus vehicle and CDC20 mRNA/protein staining increased in expanded human progenitors versus hepatocytes. These are untreated injury/expansion comparisons. No drug-arm CDC20 engagement/activity,APC/C substrate ubiquitination or target-rescue experiment is shown.",
    "BUB1B": "One of15 bioinformatic hub genes. Supplementary Table1 reports upregulation in both datasets with adjusted p=4.36e-8 for GSE38941 and9.39e-3 for GSE180226. No BUBR1 protein/activity or Apcin-induced BUB1B change is shown.",
    "checkpoint_function": "No SAC function,mitotic timing,chromosome segregation,aneuploidy,micronuclei or faithful-daughter assay shown. Authors cite prior Apcin APC/C-dependent ubiquitination inhibition; that is mechanistic background,not directly measured liver target engagement.",
    "Figure7C_E": "Only CCl4/ALF versus vehicle, n3; no Apcin arm. Hub/progenitor increases and Cps1/Cyp3a11/Cyp7a1 decreases are injury associations,not drug reversal.",
    "Figure6_and_supplement": "Human hepatocyte-to-progenitor expansion and injury/vehicle expression comparisons; no Apcin intervention. The expansion medium is a multi-factor chemical/cytokine culture condition,not a genetic CDC20 restoration experiment.",
    "culture_condition_agents": [
